sections.s2_technical:
`Optional.stream()` is the bridge between Optional and Stream worlds. Before Java 9, converting a stream of Optionals to a stream of present values required the verbose `filter(Optional::isPresent).map(Optional::get)` pattern.

```java
// BEFORE Java 9: verbose
List<BigDecimal> amounts = trades.stream()
    .map(this::tryParseAmount)              // Stream<Optional<BigDecimal>>
    .filter(Optional::isPresent)             // keep only present
    .map(Optional::get)                      // unwrap
    .toList();

// AFTER Java 9: clean
List<BigDecimal> amounts = trades.stream()
    .map(this::tryParseAmount)              // Stream<Optional<BigDecimal>>
    .flatMap(Optional::stream)               // present → Stream.of(v), empty → gone
    .toList();
// One line replaces two. No .get() call — safer.
```

`Optional.or(Supplier<Optional<T>>)` provides a fallback Optional when the first is empty. Unlike `orElse` which returns a VALUE, `or` returns another OPTIONAL — enabling chaining of multiple Optional-returning methods.

```java
// Try primary source. If empty, try secondary. If empty, try tertiary.
Optional<Account> account = findInSavings(accountId)
    .or(() -> findInCurrent(accountId))     // lazy: only called if savings is empty
    .or(() -> findInNRI(accountId));         // lazy: only called if current is also empty

// orElse returns a VALUE: Optional<Account> → Account
Account a = findInSavings(id).orElse(defaultAccount);

// or returns an OPTIONAL: Optional<Account> → Optional<Account>
Optional<Account> o = findInSavings(id).or(() -> findInCurrent(id));
// Still Optional — can chain more operations (map, filter, ifPresent)
```

`Optional.ifPresentOrElse(action, emptyAction)` handles both present and empty cases with one method call.

```java
// BEFORE Java 9:
if (account.isPresent()) {
    processAccount(account.get());
} else {
    log.warn("Account not found");
}

// AFTER Java 9:
account.ifPresentOrElse(
    this::processAccount,                    // action if present
    () -> log.warn("Account not found"));    // action if empty
// One method call, no isPresent()+get() pattern
```

